    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 38900,
    pros: [
      "Double-layer latex core is meaningfully more burst resistant than single-layer budget hoses",
      "Solid brass fittings rather than plastic, which is the most common failure point on cheap expandables",
      "Extra-strength 3750D woven jacket resisted abrasion better than most competitors in our dragging test",
      "Weighs a fraction of a conventional hose and coils to roughly a third of its extended length",
      "Included shut-off valve at the nozzle end makes depressurizing quick and easy",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Still not suitable for dragging over rough gravel or concrete regularly",
      "Flow rate is lower than a 5/8-inch conventional hose at the same pressure",
      "Needs full drainage and shade storage to reach its potential lifespan",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The expandable hose we would buy. Double latex and brass fittings address the two things that kill this category, and it survived our season of testing intact.",
    description:
      "The expandable hose category is defined by its failure modes, and Flexi Hose is built to address the two biggest ones directly. The inner tube is a double layer of latex rather than the single layer used in budget hoses, which meaningfully raises burst resistance and, more importantly, means a small pinhole in one layer does not immediately end the hose. In our testing this was the only hose in the group to survive a full season of regular use plus deliberate abuse without a burst. The fittings are the other half of the story. Cheap expandable hoses almost universally use plastic couplings, which crack from the repeated stress of the hose expanding and contracting against them and from being tightened onto a spigot. Flexi Hose uses solid brass, and after a season of connecting and disconnecting there was no visible deformation or leakage at either end. The included shut-off valve at the nozzle end is more useful than it sounds, since depressurizing the hose is the single most important habit for making one last, and having a valve right there makes it easy. The honest limits are inherent to the category. Flow through the narrower expandable core is lower than a 5/8-inch conventional hose, so sprinklers run weaker. The woven jacket abrades if you drag it across rough surfaces regularly. And it will not survive being stored full of water in freezing weather.",
  },
  {
    id: "thefitlife-expandable",
    name: "TheFitLife Flexible Expandable Hose",
    category: "Triple Latex Core, 3750D Jacket, Solid Brass",
    badge: "Best Heavy Duty",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 27600,
    pros: [
      "Triple-layer latex core provides the highest burst resistance of any expandable hose we tested",
