      "The most durable expandable hose we tested. If you have burst one before and want to try again, this is the construction to buy.",
    description:
      "If the standing objection to expandable hoses is that they burst, TheFitLife is the most direct engineering answer available. Its inner tube uses three layers of latex rather than the one or two used elsewhere, which raises the pressure at which the tube fails and provides redundancy if one layer develops a weak point. In our pressure testing it took the most abuse of any hose in the group before showing any sign of stress, and it handled being left pressurized on a hot afternoon, which is the specific condition that kills most expandables, without incident. The jacket is equally serious. At 3750 denier with a visibly denser weave than budget hoses, it resisted abrasion noticeably better during our dragging tests, showing surface fuzzing rather than the thread breakage that appeared on cheaper jackets. The solid brass fittings are heavy walled and include a shut-off valve, and after repeated connection cycles they showed no deformation. What you give up is some of the category advantage. Three layers of latex plus a heavy jacket means this is a noticeably heavier and bulkier expandable hose than single-layer competitors, which narrows the weight gap to a lightweight conventional hose. It also costs more. And it remains a latex product, meaning heat, UV, and freezing all shorten its life regardless of how many layers it has.",
  },
