    name: "GrowGreen Expandable Garden Hose",
    category: "Double Latex Core, Polyester Jacket, Brass",
    badge: "Best Value",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.3,
    reviewCount: 19400,
    pros: [
      "Double latex core and brass fittings at a price closer to budget single-layer hoses",
      "Includes an 8-pattern spray nozzle, which most competitors sell separately",
      "Light and compact, coiling into a very small bundle for storage",
      "Expanded reliably to close to its rated length at typical household pressure",
      "Good customer support reputation for warranty claims within the category",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Jacket weave is lighter than premium options and shows wear sooner",
      "Included nozzle is functional but not durable long term",
      "Flow rate is on the lower end of the group",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The sensible budget pick that does not cut the two corners that matter. Double latex and brass at a price that makes replacement painless.",
    description:
      "The difficulty with budget expandable hoses is that manufacturers save money in exactly the two places that determine lifespan: single-layer latex instead of double, and plastic fittings instead of brass. GrowGreen avoids both while still landing at a price closer to the budget end of the category, which makes it the value pick in a field where value usually means disposable. In our testing it performed solidly through a season of normal use, expanding reliably to near its rated length and showing no leaks at the couplings. The included eight-pattern spray nozzle is a genuine bonus, since most hoses in this category ship bare and a decent nozzle costs a meaningful fraction of the hose price. The nozzle itself is functional rather than durable, and we would expect to replace it before the hose, but having one in the box on day one is worth something. Where it gives ground to the premium options is the jacket. The weave is lighter than the 3750D fabric on Flexi Hose and TheFitLife, and after repeated dragging across a concrete path it showed thread wear sooner. Flow rate also measured toward the lower end of the group, which is noticeable when running a sprinkler rather than hand watering. For a homeowner who wants a light, compact hose for a patio or small garden and accepts that expandables are semi-consumable, it is the sensible choice.",
  },
  {
    id: "gardguard-expandable",
    name: "Gardguard Expandable Garden Hose",
    category: "Double Latex Core, 3750D Jacket, Brass",
    badge: "Best for Small Gardens",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.3,
    reviewCount: 23100,
    pros: [
      "Available in shorter 25 and 50-foot lengths that suit patios and small gardens",
      "Double latex core with a dense 3750D jacket at a competitive price",
      "Very compact when contracted, storing easily in a small container or on a hook",
      "Solid brass fittings with a smooth-operating shut-off valve",
